      "story_id": "US-001",
      "revision_id": "R1",
      "title": "beacon-v1.4.6-anti-drift-skill-contracts-and-enforced-decision-surfaces",
      "priority": "medium",
      "status": "accepted",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "AC-001",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "Beacon v1.4.6 冻结统一的 `Skill Anatomy v2`",
          "text": "Beacon freezes a `Skill Anatomy v2` baseline for key host-visible skills with explicit sections for usage boundary, workflow or decision loop, rationalization risk, verification, evidence, state, and gate semantics.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "accepted",
          "implemented_by_run_id": "run-20260513T222411136137",
          "verified_by_run_id": "run-20260514T002632744979",
          "accepted_at": "2026-05-13T16:26:39.585421+00:00",
          "changed_in_revision": "R1",
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.6/user-story/beacon-v1.4.6-anti-drift-skill-contracts-and-enforced-decision-surfaces.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-002",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "关键 host-visible skills 具备显式 anti-rationalization sections",
          "text": "`using-beacon`, `beacon-prd`, `beacon-change`, `beacon-brainstorm`, `beacon-implement`, `beacon-qa`, and `beacon-release` all include explicit anti-rationalization guidance instead of relying on implied operator discipline.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "accepted",
          "implemented_by_run_id": "run-20260513T222411136137",
          "verified_by_run_id": "run-20260514T002632744979",
          "accepted_at": "2026-05-13T16:26:39.585421+00:00",
          "changed_in_revision": "R1",
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.6/user-story/beacon-v1.4.6-anti-drift-skill-contracts-and-enforced-decision-surfaces.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-003",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "support surface 的 non-truth / non-gate boundary 被统一写入 public contract",
          "text": "Beacon defines one unified support-surface constitution for `brainstorm`, `deep`, `ceo-review`, `design-review`, `help`, `status`, and `doctor`, and that constitution preserves `not truth source`, `not gate source`, and `not new lifecycle stage`.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "accepted",
          "implemented_by_run_id": "run-20260513T222411136137",
          "verified_by_run_id": "run-20260514T002632744979",
          "accepted_at": "2026-05-13T16:26:39.585421+00:00",
          "changed_in_revision": "R1",
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.6/user-story/beacon-v1.4.6-anti-drift-skill-contracts-and-enforced-decision-surfaces.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-004",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "high-risk decision challenge 的最小输出合同被正式定义",
          "text": "high-risk challenge output is formalized so review-style surfaces can challenge decisions, but the result must map back to route, evidence, state, or gate impact instead of ending as free-form commentary.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "accepted",
          "implemented_by_run_id": "run-20260513T222411136137",
          "verified_by_run_id": "run-20260514T002632744979",
          "accepted_at": "2026-05-13T16:26:39.585421+00:00",
          "changed_in_revision": "R1",
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.6/user-story/beacon-v1.4.6-anti-drift-skill-contracts-and-enforced-decision-surfaces.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-005",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "challenge 结果能映射回 evidence / state / gate impact",
          "text": "Beacon formalizes a public surface family model that distinguishes truth surfaces, execution surfaces, support surfaces, and gate surfaces with clear escalation and handoff boundaries.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "accepted",
          "implemented_by_run_id": "run-20260513T222411136137",
          "verified_by_run_id": "run-20260514T002632744979",
          "accepted_at": "2026-05-13T16:26:39.585421+00:00",
          "changed_in_revision": "R1",
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.6/user-story/beacon-v1.4.6-anti-drift-skill-contracts-and-enforced-decision-surfaces.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-006",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "Beacon 的 orchestration constitution 正式表达 public/support/truth/gate 分层",
          "text": "machine-checkable anti-drift enforcement is defined for the new contract baseline so missing sections, overreaching support surfaces, or unbound challenge outputs can be detected automatically.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "accepted",
          "implemented_by_run_id": "run-20260513T222411136137",
          "verified_by_run_id": "run-20260514T002632744979",
          "accepted_at": "2026-05-13T16:26:39.585421+00:00",
          "changed_in_revision": "R1",
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.6/user-story/beacon-v1.4.6-anti-drift-skill-contracts-and-enforced-decision-surfaces.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-007",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "anti-drift contract 至少具备 lint/check 级 machine enforcement 设计",
          "text": "the v1.4.6 contract preserves Beacon's philosophy-first skill design and does not regress into step-by-step operation scripts for strong models.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "accepted",
          "implemented_by_run_id": "run-20260513T222411136137",
          "verified_by_run_id": "run-20260514T002632744979",
          "accepted_at": "2026-05-13T16:26:39.585421+00:00",
          "changed_in_revision": "R1",
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.6/user-story/beacon-v1.4.6-anti-drift-skill-contracts-and-enforced-decision-surfaces.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-008",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "v1.4.6 没有把 Beacon 退化成 script-first skill pack",
          "text": "Beacon absorbs external workflow-skill methods as internal contract design, anti-rationalization, and orchestration patterns without creating a runtime dependency on external skill packs.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "accepted",
          "implemented_by_run_id": "run-20260513T222411136137",
          "verified_by_run_id": "run-20260514T002632744979",
          "accepted_at": "2026-05-13T16:26:39.585421+00:00",
          "changed_in_revision": "R1",
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.6/user-story/beacon-v1.4.6-anti-drift-skill-contracts-and-enforced-decision-surfaces.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-009",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "外部开源方法被蒸馏为内部 contract，而不是默认 runtime dependency",
          "text": "`brainstorm` and `change` remain distinct: `brainstorm` can sharpen options and framing, but only `change` can promote requirement truth intended for downstream implementation and QA.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "accepted",
          "implemented_by_run_id": "run-20260513T222411136137",
          "verified_by_run_id": "run-20260514T002632744979",
          "accepted_at": "2026-05-13T16:26:39.585421+00:00",
          "changed_in_revision": "R1",
          "story_id": "",
          "details": [],
          "source": "user-story:docs/beacon/v1.4.6/user-story/beacon-v1.4.6-anti-drift-skill-contracts-and-enforced-decision-surfaces.md"
        },
        {
          "id": "AC-010",
          "kind": "ac",
          "theme": "`brainstorm` 到 `change/prd` 的 promotion boundary 更清楚且可执行",
          "text": "the new anti-drift contract is documented as a host-visible behavior upgrade for Beacon rather than a new lifecycle stage or a replacement for existing truth, evidence, and gate governance.",
          "required": true,
          "status": "accepted",
          "implemented_by_run_id": "run-20260513T222411136137",
          "verified_by_run_id": "run-20260514T002632744979",
